1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,800
Injection happens when an app mixes user input into a command. It is like a form where someone writes an instruction in the name box, and the clerk obeys.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:17,150
In SQL, a quote mark in a name can change the query's meaning.

3
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:27,325
The same mistake appears with system commands, templates and search queries: user input mixed into instructions.

4
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:33,670
The fix is always the same idea: keep data separate from instructions.

5
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:43,030
Parameterised queries send the command and the values separately, so a value is never run as code.

6
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:49,680
Validate input, and give the database account only the permissions it needs.

